From 5c067c245a5b537f9f38ed565081686437e6bb1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Phase1 Draft (Claude, for Terhi review)" <draft@local>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(model+sim): MODEL SEMANTICS CHANGE, gated on sign-off
 -- spatial_window is now a REAL length, symmetric across all three legs.
 Pairs are kept iff max(|dx|, |dy|) <= ws in REAL coordinates (a real-space
 square; previously Euclidean in INTERNAL units, so the truncation region was
 a preprocessing-dependent ellipse in real space and applied on the EVENT side
 only). The compensator charges the truncation EXACTLY: with the kernel
 already real-unit (previous commit) its limits are real distances, so the ws
 clip is a SCALAR jnp.minimum -- the perfect per-axis mirror of min(T - t, w)
 temporally, and the reason this patch lands AFTER the kernel realification
 rather than before it (an internal-unit ws clip would have been a per-axis
 vector rewritten one commit later). Offspring thinning applies the identical
 rule on the real-unit draw. The predicate is SINGLE-SOURCED
 (utils.within_real_box_window, shared by the pair mask and the thinning; the
 compensator clip is its exact integral) so the three legs cannot drift -- the
 Phase 2b lesson. Box (not disc) semantics retained from the withdrawn 2c
 draft: disc-intersect-rectangle has no closed-form Gaussian mass, so disc
 truncation can never be charged exactly. test_pairs' dense reference oracle
 updated to the same semantics with unequal-scale coverage (test edit, part of
 the signed-off change). THREE identities land: (I4-ws) per-parent cascade
 mean m/(1-m) with m = alpha*F_beta(w)*BoxMass(ws) through the production
 atom, and (I11-ws) conservation with spatial_window=0.2 -- both IMPOSSIBLE
 before the symmetry (event-side-only truncation); and NEW identity (I12, box
 invariance): one real dataset ingested under two differently-shaped
 rectangles must agree on the pair set, the real-unit displacements and kernel
 densities, the ws-clipped compensator, and byte-identical seeded offspring
 cascades. (I12) is the operational statement that the trigger no longer
 depends on the bounding-box preprocessing choice; verified RED on the pre-fix
 code at its first clause (33 vs 68 pairs across a 4:1 and a 3:1 box at
 ws=0.15). Requires ws to exceed the kernel scale in REAL units (docstring
 rule of thumb: ws >= 4*sqrt(sigmax_2)); user-facing docstrings updated
 (spatial_window is exact likelihood now, safe for calibration/SBC). Verified:
 46/46; value+gradient pins BIT-IDENTICAL across all four pin configs
 (spatial_window=None in every pinned config; the ws=None paths are
 op-identical); ruff clean.

